    push(make(`${base}-word`,'act','act-read-craft',d,`As it is used in the passage, the word “${item.word}” most nearly means`,[item.meaning,'physical size or weight','public celebration','complete disagreement'],0,'The surrounding context supports the precise meaning in the correct choice.',extra));
    push(make(`${base}-structure`,'act','act-read-craft',Math.min(4,d+1),'Which choice best describes the overall organization of the passage?',[item.structure,'It states a claim and then repeats that claim in different words without evidence.','It lists unrelated examples in chronological order and leaves them uninterpreted.','It presents two identical positions and argues that no distinction exists between them.'],0,'The correct choice follows the passage’s actual sequence and explains how its parts develop the central idea.',extra));
    push(make(`${base}-evidence`,'act','act-read-integration',Math.min(4,d+1),'Which choice best explains how one piece of evidence functions in the passage?',[item.evidence,'The evidence proves that the result must occur in every setting.','The evidence is presented as irrelevant to the passage’s recommendation.','The evidence replaces the need to consider any limitation mentioned later.'],0,'The correct choice connects a specific observation to the claim it supports without overstating the result.',extra));
    push(make(`${base}-qualify`,'act','act-read-integration',Math.min(4,d+1),'Which choice best describes an important qualification made by the passage?',[item.qualification,'The passage withdraws its central idea and offers no alternative interpretation.','The passage reports that every variable and outcome was controlled perfectly.','The passage treats one example as sufficient to establish a universal rule.'],0,'The correct choice identifies a genuine boundary or complication that makes the passage’s reasoning more precise.',extra));
